-# Inline knowledge card (index-page help pattern — see CLAUDE.md).
.card.border-0.shadow-sm.border-start.border-4.border-info
  .card-body.p-4
    .d-flex.align-items-center.mb-3
      .bg-info-subtle.text-info-emphasis.rounded-circle.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-center.me-3.lh-1{style: 'width: 48px; height: 48px'}
        %span.mi.md-24.fill healing
      %div
        %h5.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-0 About Near-Miss runs
        %small.text-secondary Bounded LLM repair as a research instrument — no effect on student scores
    .row.g-4
      .col-lg-6
        .d-flex.gap-3
          .text-info.flex-shrink-0
            %span.mi.md-24 straighten
          %div
            %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-1 Budget gate
            %p.small.text-muted.mb-0.lh-sm
              The LLM proposes the smallest fix it can; a deterministic gate
              measures it (lines and characters) against the run's budget.
              Acceptance is never the LLM's opinion.
      .col-lg-6
        .d-flex.gap-3
          .text-info.flex-shrink-0
            %span.mi.md-24 visibility_off
          %div
            %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-1 Shadow submissions
            %p.small.text-muted.mb-0.lh-sm
              Accepted patches are graded by the real judge as linked shadow
              submissions — invisible to students and excluded from every
              score and quota.
      .col-lg-6
        .d-flex.gap-3
          .text-info.flex-shrink-0
            %span.mi.md-24 trending_up
          %div
            %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-1 Rescued &amp; mechanical gap
            %p.small.text-muted.mb-0.lh-sm
              Gap = repaired − original score. A positive gap is a rescue; a
              negative gap means the repair broke working code — the key
              safety signal when comparing models.
      .col-lg-6
        .d-flex.gap-3
          .text-info.flex-shrink-0
            %span.mi.md-24 terminal
          %div
            %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-1 CSV export
            %p.small.text-muted.mb-0.lh-sm
              %code rake near_miss:report RUN=&lt;label&gt;
              prints the same per-problem tables and writes a CSV under
              %code tmp/
              for offline analysis.
